# Campaign Tracker — copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     $EDITOR .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored (see .gitignore) — a real key pasted there can never
# be committed by accident. `run.sh` sources this file automatically; if
# you're not using run.sh, `export` the same three variables by hand, or use
# `set -a; source .env; set +a` yourself before `python3 app.py`.
#
# See CLAUDE.md's "If someone just asked you to help them set this up"
# section for the full walkthrough, including what each stage needs.

# --- 1. FEC key (money side). Free, instant self-service signup: -----------
#        https://api.open.fec.gov/developers/
FEC_API_KEY=

# --- 2. Congress key (legislative record + votes). Free, same key system ---
#        also covers Congress.gov: https://api.data.gov/signup/
CONGRESS_API_KEY=

# --- 3. SearXNG (statement gathering) — optional. ---------------------------
#        Use the SAME URL your SearXNG web UI opens at in the browser;
#        common default is http://localhost:8080. Set up an instance via
#        docker/searxng/ (see docker/searxng/README.md) or leave this blank —
#        that one stage is disclosed-and-skipped, money + legislative record
#        + votes still run complete.
SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:8080

# The Anthropic key (translation layer / plain-language report) deliberately
# does NOT go here. Paste it into the "Anthropic API key" field in the web UI
# for each run instead — it's used for that request only and is never
# stored, so there's nothing in this file to remember to scrub before
# sharing the folder.
